        {
            "id": "c039fe2e-9796-47d8-99bc-11f0f99a72ca",
            "build_id": "e1d61900-8372-4a8d-a468-7890cded6137",
            "round_number": 7,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-10-04T05:49:45.191378+00:00",
            "notes": "I typically grab [Sonic Boom](item_e0a58a96-c17f-4c99-ba06-8daaa5fd5508) in round seven.  It makes it so every method of attack I have in my aggressive play is healing my nearby teammates.  I also like [Radio Edit](item_cd4b345d-19ff-4a91-917e-b133fe5ba4c2) as an option but find my healing output go down while mitigation comes up.  Up to you.  [Radio Edit](item_cd4b345d-19ff-4a91-917e-b133fe5ba4c2) is cool, loud and flashy, but I prefer the subtle constant healing from [Sonic Boom](item_e0a58a96-c17f-4c99-ba06-8daaa5fd5508).\n\nAs for Items, trade [Nano Cola](item_79b22609-8046-4a8a-a5a2-bb49cd7e11c6) for [Champion's Kit](item_8682f8c7-8811-439b-8d50-fa81cd43ddce).  Then spend your last slot on ability power or survival.  It can vary game to game, but [Cybervenom](item_210a8582-91ec-4cf3-968a-a443f3a0c505) is always a solid choice.  Your cone AoE [Soundwave](ability_5ccc6ce6-cf44-4509-a720-b2e341261512) heals your team while simultaneously applying healing reduction to theirs.  It's a solid tide-turner to have in your back pocket for that round you absolutely must win",
